# UI conventions

Layout target: **overview first, side panel, scrolling entries** (Robinhood-style). Do not invent a new IA. `dashboard.vue` is already the logbook surface — extract components/composables instead of adding more logic to that file.

## Use what exists

- iOS secondary pages: `IosAppPageShell`
- Settings: `SettingsStackShell`, `SettingsSection`, `SettingsListGroup`, `SettingsRow` / `SettingsListRow`
- Entries: `LogEntryList` / `LogEntryCard`
- Font: `font-quicksand`. Theme: `isDarkMode` with `gray-950` / `gray-50` (and the matching border tokens already on those screens). Respect light and dark on every touched page.
- `docs/oss-ui-and-architecture-guardrails.md` names `AppPageShell` / `AppCard` — those primitives are **not** in the tree. Do not invent them; reuse the shells above.

```vue
<!-- ❌ BAD: new page with a long empty-state essay and one-off hex backgrounds -->
<p class="text-sm">Welcome to your Digifi journey! Here you can seamlessly...</p>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: short chrome, same shell as nearby screens -->
<IosAppPageShell title="Digifi Eye">
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">No scans yet.</p>
</IosAppPageShell>
```

Keep helper text optional and one line. New pages must not look like a different product.
